"Let $p\\in\\{2,3,\\ldots,8\\}$, and let $G$ be a bipartite graph with $V\\geq 2p-5$ vertices. A graph has no $K_p$-minor when $K_p$ cannot be obtained from it by taking a subgraph and contracting edges.\n\n**Bipartite excluded-minor extremal conjecture.** A bipartite graph on $V\\geq 2p-5$ vertices with no $K_p$-minor has at most\n\n$$\n(p-2)V-(p-2)^2\n$$\n\nedges.\n\nThis conjecture extends the known extremal bounds for graphs excluding complete-graph minors to bipartite graphs through $p=8$. Its resolution is not supplied in the source."